{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0263","math_ordinal":44,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Without parentheses the indexed epsilon term lies outside the sum and leaves n free; grouping it gives the printed next equality because the geometric series sums to 2.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:85-88","source_normalized_sha256":"438e8b40cde83c9a34fcb447b87ed0463e6557b3ab50a7edc026682abfba55dc","source_text":"$\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\\theta_{r\\delta}A_n+2^{-n}\\epsilon$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:84-87","target_normalized_sha256":"a4cde3d38b7a8e8546526a035edc1743f40bab153fc09e085d564d9c6eca31f6","target_text":"$\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}(\\theta_{r\\delta}A_n+2^{-n}\\epsilon)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-bound-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0264","math_ordinal":117,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The union binds n and the covering sequence is A_n; k is unbound in this statement.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:180","source_normalized_sha256":"7e33753cd544d0e256214f4addf5b07d3bf00d12412364bb108fb452472af02e","source_text":"$A\\subseteq\\bigcup_{n\\in K}A_k$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:175","target_normalized_sha256":"f40ad577e084639546e230583f62fc6dda7cda63954fd793ac6101929a53c981","target_text":"$A\\subseteq\\bigcup_{n\\in K}A_n$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-index-case","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0265","math_ordinal":131,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The subsequent union and series use every natural-number index; n>1 leaves B_1 undefined, while the same formula is valid and required for n=1.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:205-206","source_normalized_sha256":"f6283b2d053942151249b9a150b6e4011308eda0a614de940c5eff3d3b26663d","source_text":"$B_n=A_n\\setminus A_{n-1}$ for $n>1$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:200-201","target_normalized_sha256":"67500429cdd36beba6a6b015ccfa15bb06e8ef7a54ae4a5c55ec9349fa45c1ea","target_text":"$B_n=A_n\\setminus A_{n-1}$ untuk $n>0$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-summand-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0266","math_ordinal":152,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Convergence of the series gives a small tail indexed by n; the printed B_m repeats a constant term and contradicts the next displayed line.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:225-226","source_normalized_sha256":"5500d738646776138b0c3cb75f3d6bb7a4960e2f0c5752e318c536cff18a084b","source_text":"$\\sum_{n=m}^{\\infty}\\theta_rB_m\\le\\epsilon$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:220-221","target_normalized_sha256":"f9a07f233f57362b5b62d866a0a62ac93829a6ff7c0b49bd83068e5476b8a488","target_text":"$\\sum_{n=m}^{\\infty}\\theta_rB_n\\le\\epsilon$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-transposed-cover-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0267","math_ordinal":190,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The cover chosen for each fixed n is the sequence A_nm; the closures F_nm and every following estimate retain that order.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:271-272","source_normalized_sha256":"661329bab5060b53de595431310d3f275b988ad83a487ed8829b3a9184195149","source_text":"$\\bigcap_n\\bigcup_m A_{mn}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:266-267","target_normalized_sha256":"ce3921f1e52956b0ea5cd1a47b829468537fea58665034e28924a6ba524026be","target_text":"$\\bigcap_n\\bigcup_m A_{nm}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-function-outside-domain","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0268","math_ordinal":260,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"phi is defined only on D and the preceding cover correctly uses phi[A_n intersect D]; the un-intersected image may be undefined.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:375-377","source_normalized_sha256":"16f18dc489a168aa053901b3053d13cd607b0235135c727c55b4ccf358cc5c44","source_text":"$(\\diam\\phi[A_n])^r$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:371-373","target_normalized_sha256":"d0fdbd6b5ed621dbf4f376933e0db888e1949120b1630066658df28c8685066a","target_text":"$(\\diam\\phi[A_n\\cap D])^r$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-ambient-space","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0269","math_ordinal":294,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The set is acted on by r-coordinate reflections and measured by r-dimensional Lebesgue outer measure, so it lies in R^r.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:435","source_normalized_sha256":"60f2525df72112cd960fada3bdfd2fafdedb653246bfa36eee6ec4ab757d4765","source_text":"$C\\subseteq\\Bbb R$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:428","target_normalized_sha256":"1c931dc4e429819f2840e09427535e9ee6aadee7616cb85390a34228c985cb80","target_text":"$C\\subseteq\\Bbb R^r$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-induction-case","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0270","math_ordinal":485,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"After the base case l=0 the next case is l=1; the stated recursive split is valid for every positive l and otherwise leaves that case unproved.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:694-700","source_normalized_sha256":"c47c378089dd44c97bf2cf53c664d16a36a09aeb029a7f6553f863dc9794c7ca","source_text":"inductive step to $l>1$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:692-698","target_normalized_sha256":"a6eafa8e90b1ea84e7fea52517125d4be6bc5b13ef977e4aed7f0f5c9709f2a6","target_text":"langkah induksi menuju $l>0$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-ambient-space","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0271","math_ordinal":565,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Exercise 264Xc declares A as a subset of R^s and defines no space X; both covering classes must use the declared ambient Euclidean space.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:793-803","source_normalized_sha256":"9afa62653ba152fb85f00d055c9cb5e4bc91b7736a5b25ca71d21169c672e7f9","source_text":"closed/open subsets of $X$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:792-802","target_normalized_sha256":"dc324a8ec74ac573dd46bbbd428dc1959a57a6bbb03733690088041622854425","target_text":"subhimpunan tertutup/terbuka dari $\\Bbb R^s$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-graph-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0272","math_ordinal":587,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The exercise defines the graph only as Gamma_f; bare Gamma is not introduced.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:817-820","source_normalized_sha256":"57885e4c75965b23b196228446c46b00876b0951643235b678d18199f6dce5ec","source_text":"outer measure of $\\Gamma$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:815-819","target_normalized_sha256":"e5e2347167ec97cffbc5c45d05d29896bd33f3bcbcc696a0e2abaad4fa2f260b","target_text":"ukuran luar dari $\\Gamma_f$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-omitted-first-interval","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0273","math_ordinal":770,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The ordered family contains intervals indexed 0 through n, so absolute continuity must sum the image distances over the same complete index range.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:982","source_normalized_sha256":"9d5b7100c03512391597b5dfbf58e7b2259c2b97f0224d3ea0d5380348c3244d","source_text":"$\\sum_{i=1}^n\\rho(f(a_i),f(b_i))$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:979","target_normalized_sha256":"1f2444f1c92915f1c462901398ba9ed4970e9a32fe0a69ec410f7c7efb598e68","target_text":"$\\sum_{i=0}^n\\rho(f(a_i),f(b_i))$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0274","math_ordinal":772,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Absolute continuity bounds the sum of interval lengths; without parentheses only b_i is summed and a_i remains free.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:984","source_normalized_sha256":"e346d589f0b04dbd4ea39c7a60037e4b85ba492690241ec61ce4f97f02276215","source_text":"$\\sum_{i=0}^nb_i-a_i$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:981","target_normalized_sha256":"923732aa78f03589502286457fb41b74aae22e19d5636abcf60f1e1e04457a28","target_text":"$\\sum_{i=0}^n(b_i-a_i)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-metric-range-condition","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0275","math_ordinal":780,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The snowflake exponent s/r must be at most one for the triangle inequality; r>=s is necessary, while the printed range admits counterexamples such as s=2 and r=1.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:992-994","source_normalized_sha256":"2a505fb82a4b3da7eff6ecc9465939b47b82b8e6ef0134ab035ede45e910af99","source_text":"$r\\in\\coint{1,\\infty}$ and $\\rho(x,y)=\\|x-y\\|^{s/r}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:989-992","target_normalized_sha256":"38df5bf09772b2a1b09f507618d86ec8bead11f5cf89d42c04c664a43fea9736","target_text":"$r\\in\\coint{s,\\infty}$ and $\\rho(x,y)=\\|x-y\\|^{s/r}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-measure-notation-mismatch","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0286","math_ordinal":238,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proposition and displayed inequality concern Hausdorff outer measure, whose notation here is mu_Hr-star; unstarred mu_Hr denotes the completed measure.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:348-350","source_normalized_sha256":"e743fe8316fcff8f2d9538efb00d23bbd8328edc5fe4cd44d96c16d433de340e","source_text":"writing $\\mu_{Hr}$ for r-dimensional Hausdorff outer measure","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:344-346","target_normalized_sha256":"a61d01bd48d04401672926f34069683792fa2f156826b176ebbaa2de67775e47","target_text":"menuliskan $\\mu_{Hr}^*$ untuk ukuran luar Hausdorff berdimensi $r$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-domain-hypothesis","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0287","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Because phi is defined only on D, phi[E] is not defined for arbitrary E; the conclusion requires E to be a subset of D.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:923-925","source_text":"if X is complete and $\\mu_{Hr}E$ is defined and finite, then $\\mu_{Hr}(\\phi[E])$ is defined","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:920-922","target_normalized_sha256":"809f6da7c90f034888299fe2f4046fe685f1865181f2236e7b0aee02758f9c67","target_text":"jika $X$ lengkap dan $E\\subseteq D$ dan $\\mu_{Hr}E$ terdefinisi dan berhingga, maka $\\mu_{Hr}(\\phi[E])$ terdefinisi","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-zero-normalization","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0288","math_ordinal":753,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Without h(0)=0 the construction need not send the empty set to zero; for example h identically one gives theta_h(emptyset)=infinity, so it is not an outer measure.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt264.tex:962-964","source_normalized_sha256":"8b64a4873017d277b6e9915b45d04f09c132178f90cc3a73e057dc98f883f0e3","source_text":"$h:\\coint{0,\\infty}\\to\\coint{0,\\infty}$ a non-decreasing function","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt264.tex:959-961","target_normalized_sha256":"888ee3e42b2b3d00d1c16e23b7f1af9477ff62652afb562db2e67499c1fdaea0","target_text":"$h:\\coint{0,\\infty}\\to\\coint{0,\\infty},\\ h(0)=0$ suatu fungsi tak menurun","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S264"}
